      "context": [
        {
          "id": 13,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "At first light we break camp and ride on north."
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "name": "Adolion Narrator",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "*First light bleeds grey across the sky when the party breaks camp, leaving nothing behind but a ring of cold stones.*\nThe road remains unsettlingly clear. By midday, they come upon the first sign of what Tobias had warned about: an overturned carriage, its wheels shattered and cargo still strapped down. A dead horse lies in the road beside it, but no signs of a struggle—no blood spatter or scattered belongings. Just a vehicle left where it failed, and nobody who came back to retrieve it.\n*Belle pulls her horse to a stop, eyes narrowing as she surveys the wreckage.* \"Something's wrong,\" *she says quietly.* \"People don't just leave their coin and gear on the road. Not unless they're dead or scared.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "We follow the riderless horse's tracks north toward Wendhope."
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "name": "Giada",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "*A flash of movement near the treeline catches Giada's eye—a silhouette against the dim grey light. She doesn't call out. Instead, she melts into the shadows between the pines, her pale skin nearly translucent in the gloom. Her navy cloak blends with the underbrush as she follows the riderless horse at a distance, her bare feet making no sound on the frost-touched earth.*\n*She stops behind a thick oak, watching the strange company. Three adventurers. One noble with shadows clinging to them, an elf with a bow, and a human woman with an axe. Giada's ice-blue eyes track the horse, then flicker to the abandoned carriage. No blood. No struggle. Her lips thin into a flat line.*\n*She says nothing, her breath hardly misting in the cold. She simply watches and waits, her hand resting lightly on the hilt of the crystalline dagger at her hip. If they're fools who will wander right into a demon's maw, she'll let them. If they're something else...*"
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "Who's that pale woman by the pines? Belle, Dalan, eyes on her. We reach the walls and call out to the gate."
        }
      ],
      "contextFrom": "event-time"
    }
  ],
